    <item>
      <title>Whitney&amp;#039;s Birthday - Jeff&amp;#039;s ACWW Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/18/whitneys-birthday/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/18/whitneys-birthday/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 03:58:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-9017" class="post-9017 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Whitney&amp;#8217;s Birthday&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	 	 	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Yesterday, I received a letter from Wishy in the mail. It was about the shooting star I wished on last week. He &amp;#8220;granted my wish&amp;#8221; by sending me a dracaena. I&amp;#8217;m not sure that&amp;#8217;s quite what I wished for, but a free gift is a free gift.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Pippy was talking about the Bug-Off that&amp;#8217;s coming up on Sunday. She told me she has a bite-proof dress that (somehow?) keeps the bugs from biting her.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/pippy-bite.jpg" alt="Pippy: I got this cute bite-proof dress to keep the bugs from taking revenge on me." class="wp-image-9018" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;Tell me your secret. Mosquitos keep biting me!&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Maple was finally over her cold that she&amp;#8217;s had for the past couple weeks. She thanked me for the medicine by giving me a watermelon table. &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/maple-miserable.jpg" alt="Maple: If it weren't you for, I'd still be curled up in bed, feeling miserable!" class="wp-image-9019" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;I&amp;#8217;m glad you&amp;#8217;re not feeling melon-choly now!&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I visited Whitney, I found a pack of wolves inside her house. 😉 It was her birthday, and she was celebrating with Chief.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/whitney-bday.jpg" alt="Whitney: Well, well, look who it is. Welcome to Whitney's Birthday Bash, fribbit!" class="wp-image-9020" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;For a gift, I gave her the Nintendo bench that I bought from Pippy on the last &lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/05/better-call-sell/"&gt;Flea Market day&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/whitney-bench.jpg" alt="Whitney: Oh, look at this! It's just what I've always wanted! A Nintendo bench." class="wp-image-9021" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I played again tonight, and Derwin told me one of his darkest secrets: He likes clothes with fringes! 😆&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/derwin-fringes.jpg" alt="Derwin: It's one of my darkest secrets, but...I'm actually into clothes with fringes." class="wp-image-9022" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Whitney wanted to have a competition to see who could catch a bell cricket first, and I actually agreed to the battle. Whitney assured me that she wouldn&amp;#8217;t lose to a loser like me. 🙄&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/whitney-loser.jpg" alt="Whitney: Tee hee! I'll never lose to a loser like you!" class="wp-image-9023" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;So I went around looking for crickets, and there were plenty of them. Unfortunately, the vast majority were regular crickets, not bell crickets! After catching several of the wrong ones, I had to hunt by sound and listen for the different call of the bell crickets. It took me seven and a half minutes, but I finally caught one!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/bell-cricket.jpg" alt="I caught a bell cricket! He's the littlest musician!" class="wp-image-9024" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;By that point, I was afraid Whitney would&amp;#8217;ve already caught one. (Or at least &lt;em&gt;claimed&lt;/em&gt; to.) But fortunately, she didn&amp;#8217;t. I gave her the bug, and she handed over a parlor wall as my prize for winning. But she wasn&amp;#8217;t happy about losing to me. Too bad, wolf girl.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/whitney-thumbs.jpg" alt="Whitney: I lost to you?! Those opposable thumbs you have really help, huh?" class="wp-image-9025" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;Excuses, excuses.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;After selling the remaining crickets and mosquitos in my pockets, I went to town hall. There, I found a cabana lamp in the recycle bin.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Enjoy your weekend, everyone! I&amp;#8217;ll be back with another entry next week. 🙂&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;img alt='' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0ff365ea4b4ae589e18c26b092fe26946a6e14116b63065f41029c8c6138c7c8?s=98&amp;d=mm&amp;r=g' class='avatar avatar-49 photo' height='49' width='49'/&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/18/whitneys-birthday/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-18T23:58:00-04:00"&gt;September 18, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-09-19T00:43:19-04:00"&gt;September 19, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt; &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/pippy-bite.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Missing Link? - Jeff&amp;#039;s ACCF Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/09/12/missing-link/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/09/12/missing-link/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 03:58:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-14166" class="post-14166 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Missing Link?&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Scoot was sick today&amp;#8230;maybe it was from eating all that &lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/08/22/mouthful-of-ash/" data-type="post" data-id="14132"&gt;ash&lt;/a&gt; during the fireworks festival. 😉 But I gave him some medicine, so hopefully he&amp;#8217;ll start feeling better soon.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;There was a new house in town, so I went inside to meet Iggly&amp;#8217;s replacement: It was Bluebear the&amp;#8230;blue bear. 😆&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8643-sm.jpg" alt="Bluebear: Oh! Hiya! I'm Bluebear! I'm gonna, like, take the world by STORM! Tee hee!" class="wp-image-14167" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I like her, and she&amp;#8217;s an improvement over Iggly. (Sorry, Iggly.) But it&amp;#8217;ll be nice to have her around. Welcome to Forest, Bluebear!&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Big Top recently asked me for a new catchphrase, and I told him to say &amp;#8220;it&amp;#8217;s Link.&amp;#8221; I guess I&amp;#8217;m a bit excited about the Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time remake coming out in November. 😛&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;But speaking of Big Top, he asked me to play a game of hide-and-seek this afternoon. He gave me ten minutes to find him, Apollo, and Pecan. My eagle eyes led me to Apollo almost instantly. He was trying to hide behind Willow&amp;#8217;s house.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8644-sm.jpg" alt="Apollo, during a game of hide-and-seek: Well, pickle and can me! It looks like I've been found." class="wp-image-14168" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;About a minute later, I found Big Top behind a tree near Nook &amp;#8216;n&amp;#8217; Go. He told me there was only one person left to find&amp;#8230;but his catchphrase fit in quite nicely.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="499" height="280" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/accf-hidden-link.jpg" alt="Big Top: There's only one of us left for you to find? Well, good luck, it's Link!" class="wp-image-14169" sizes="(max-width: 499px) 100vw, 499px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;I&amp;#8217;ll have to find the missing Link! 😉&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;With 6+ minutes remaining on the game timer, I found Pecan next to Able Sisters. (It wasn&amp;#8217;t Link after all.) But I was surprised to see that Big Top had already shared his new catchphrase with her!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8645-sm.jpg" alt="Pecan: OH NO! Can't you pretend you didn't see me, it's Link?" class="wp-image-14170" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I won the game, and Big Top rewarded me with his mega dingloid.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Shortly after that, I wrapped up my game for the afternoon. But I returned (briefly) tonight, mainly just to check out K.K. Slider&amp;#8217;s concert. I asked him for a random song, and he performed &amp;#8220;King K.K.&amp;#8221; for me.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8646-sm.jpg" alt="K.K.: All right, get ready to dig the riffs on this ditty: King K.K.." class="wp-image-14171" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/09/12/missing-link/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-12T23:58:00-04:00"&gt;September 12, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-09-13T02:11:21-04:00"&gt;September 13, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8643-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Whitney&amp;#039;s Tune - Jeff&amp;#039;s ACWW Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/12/whitneys-tune/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/12/whitneys-tune/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 03:42:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-9006" class="post-9006 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Whitney&amp;#8217;s Tune&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	 	 	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Yesterday, Angus told me that he thinks of all the people in town, Whitney and Marina are the closest friends. He then added that he never wants to fight with me. (Frankly, I think that&amp;#8217;s a bunch of &lt;em&gt;bull&lt;/em&gt;.) 🐂&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/angus-fight.jpg" alt="Angus: Even though you bug me sometimes, I don't ever want to fight with you." class="wp-image-9007" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;Your eyes seem to say you want to fight me right now. 😛&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I noticed that my savings account balance reached 21 million bells, thanks to my monthly bank interest (plus one bell I deposited to make it a round number).&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/phyllis-21m.jpg" alt="Phyllis: Your balance is 50 billion bells. Just kidding! It's actually 21,000,000." class="wp-image-9008" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Today was La-Di-Day, and Chief was the first villager to sing for me. However, I wasn&amp;#8217;t impressed with his song.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/chief-ballad.jpg" alt="Chief: Make sure you hear my song. It's a manly country ballad, on a pig!" class="wp-image-9009" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Angus told me that &lt;em&gt;his &lt;/em&gt;best song is a ballad, and he said that &amp;#8220;hipster kids&amp;#8221; won&amp;#8217;t get it. 😛&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/angus-ballad.jpg" alt="Angus: My best song is a ballad. I don't think the hipster kids will get it." class="wp-image-9010" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;But even though I spoke with him a couple times, he didn&amp;#8217;t actually sing it for me. Oh well, you had your chance, Angus!&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;After I came out of Angus&amp;#8217;s house, I heard a shooting star! I quickly wished on it. Check back next week to see what Wishy sends me!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/wish-91226.jpg" alt="Jeff wishes on a shooting star in Animal Crossing: Wild World (ACWW) for Nintendo DS." class="wp-image-9011" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Anyway, there was only one other villager that sang a La-Di-Day song for me: Whitney.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/whitney-singing.jpg" alt="Whitney: You're about to hear a singing sensation live! Whitney, fribbit!" class="wp-image-9013" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I liked her song; it sounded unique, with several pauses. So I hired Whitney, and her song is now the official town tune of Forest. I checked the notes over at town hall, so you all can recreate it (and use it) if you&amp;#8217;d like.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/whitney-tune.jpg" alt="The notes of Whitney's song, which became the new town tune of Forest on September 12, 2026." class="wp-image-9014" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Maple has still been sick with that cold from last week, so I gave her more medicine yesterday and today. Get well soon, Maple!&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Down at the Roost, K.K. Slider performed &amp;#8220;K.K. Condor&amp;#8221; for me. That&amp;#8217;s one of my favorites! It&amp;#8217;s the o-o-o-o-o song (iykyk).&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kk-91226.jpg" alt="K.K.: All right, get ready to dig the riffs on this ditty: K.K. Condor!" class="wp-image-9012" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;img alt='' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0ff365ea4b4ae589e18c26b092fe26946a6e14116b63065f41029c8c6138c7c8?s=98&amp;d=mm&amp;r=g' class='avatar avatar-49 photo' height='49' width='49'/&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/12/whitneys-tune/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-12T23:42:00-04:00"&gt;September 12, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-09-13T01:15:45-04:00"&gt;September 13, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt; &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/angus-fight.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Singing Indoors - Jeff&amp;#039;s New Horizons Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/09/12/singing-indoors/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/09/12/singing-indoors/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 03:05:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-9684" class="post-9684 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Singing Indoors&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;On Wednesday, Savannah sneezed in my face! &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/savannah-sneeze-sm.jpg" alt="Savannah, about to sneeze: Oh! Thanks so--Ah-CHOO!--much." class="wp-image-9688" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I gave her some medicine for her cold, and she thanked me with a coverall coat.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Tucker the elephant was camping over at the campsite. He seems pretty cool, but I did not invite him to move in.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/tucker-camper-sm.jpg" alt="Tucker, at the campsite: Hi there! Are you from this island? I'm here camping." class="wp-image-9689" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;On Thursday, I caught an emperor butterfly that was flying right behind Louie. It was almost on his back! And I thought it looked funny how Louie was right there where you&amp;#8217;d expect to see me holding the bug.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/emperor-butt-sm.jpg" alt="I caught an emperor butt" class="wp-image-9690" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Yesterday, I visited Savannah and I was surprised to see her singing in her house! Normally they just sing outdoors, so this caught me by surprise.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="368" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/savannah-sing.jpg" alt="Savannah sings inside her house." class="wp-image-9686" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;My former villager Tia was in town as a tourist today, and she was looking for a place to stay for the night. I didn&amp;#8217;t feel like designing a VIP room though, so I put her in a standard room. She ended up the ice room; I hope she doesn&amp;#8217;t get cold! But she does have some thick skin, so she should be okay.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/tia-hotel-sm.jpg" alt="Tia: Lovely rooms, kind staff... This hotel is so perfect." class="wp-image-9691" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;K.K. Slider was in town tonight, and I asked him for a random song. He performed &amp;#8220;K.K. Samba&amp;#8221; for me, Bones, and Merengue.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="600" height="334" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kk-91226.jpg" alt="K.K. Slider performs for Bones, Jeff, and Merengue." class="wp-image-9687" sizes="auto, (max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Here are a few other quick notes about this week:&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;ul class="wp-block-list"&gt; &lt;li&gt;I helped out Wisp twice this week. He gave me some horizontal split curtains on Sunday and some olive Moroccan flooring on Monday.&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;On Wednesday, I sold 18 bugs to Flick for 128k.&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;I helped Gulliver on Thursday, and he sent me a Sphinx in the mail.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Earlier this week, I posted my latest New Horizons Moments video. Here it is:&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"&gt;&lt;div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper"&gt; &lt;iframe loading="lazy" title="Colton Had My Back! / New Horizons Moments #43 (Animal Crossing ACNH)" width="660" height="371" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/WCvCFn2O7A0?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/09/12/singing-indoors/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-12T23:05:00-04:00"&gt;September 12, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-09-13T00:22:10-04:00"&gt;September 13, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/savannah-sneeze-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Fishing for a Million - Jeff&amp;#039;s Animal Crossing Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/2026/09/11/fishing-for-a-million/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/2026/09/11/fishing-for-a-million/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 03:48:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-6241" class="post-6241 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Fishing for a Million&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;On Tuesday (September 8th), I unfortunately found a goodbye letter from Kiki in the mail. I&amp;#8217;m sad to see her go.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-kiki-out2026-sm.jpg" alt="Dearest Jeff, I'm moving. There, I said it. I'd tell you where I'm going, but if you were to come to visit, I...just know I'd cry. Please forgive me for going. This is how things must be. Take care! -Kiki" class="wp-image-6242" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Her replacement was Zoe the anteater, who moved into the plot next to Candi. That&amp;#8217;s the spot where Yuka once lived, many years ago! Zoe may not be my favorite, but at least she&amp;#8217;s no Yuka. 😛&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-zoe2026-sm.jpg" alt="Zoe: My name is Zoe. I hope I'll be seeing a lot more of you from now on!" class="wp-image-6243" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;It was raining in town, and Puck wasn&amp;#8217;t happy about it. He hoped that it was just a passing shower.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-puck-passing-sm.jpg" alt="Puck: Let's hope it's just a passing shower, brrrrrrrrr." class="wp-image-6244" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Of course, there&amp;#8217;s no such thing as a passing shower on GameCube. When it&amp;#8217;s a rainy day, it rains the entire day.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I took advantage of the great September fishing by catching plenty of red snappers, barred knifejaws, and several coelacanths as well (thanks to the rain).&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-coco2026-sm.jpg" alt="I caught a living fossil! I didn't know they really existed!" class="wp-image-6245" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-nook99k-sm.jpg" alt="Tom Nook: If I add it all up, my price comes to 99,000 bells. You will sell, yes?" class="wp-image-6246" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I filled my pockets up repeatedly, making over 450k in total on Tuesday.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I played again yesterday, and after Puck showed me a letter, he warned me to watch out when he&amp;#8217;s hungry. 😛&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-puck-hungry2026-sm.jpg" alt="Puck: Well, whatever. I'm hungry right now, and when I'm hungry, WATCH OUT!" class="wp-image-6248" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;Somebody needs a Snickers. 😛&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Peewee asked me to buy his skull shirt for 660 bells. Since October (and Halloween) are right around the corner, I decided to buy it and put it on. 💀&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-peewee-skull-sm.jpg" alt="Peewee: Yeah, it's a skull shirt. I'll sell it for 660 bells. What do you think?" class="wp-image-6249" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I found Gulliver down on the beach, and he gave me a free tribal mask. I wish he would give me one of those&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;in Wild World, since it&amp;#8217;s the only Gulliver item I don&amp;#8217;t have in that game.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;It wasn&amp;#8217;t raining yesterday, so there weren&amp;#8217;t any more coelacanths out. But I still did some more fishing. Unfortunately, a few sea bass have started to return. I wish there was an option to throw fish back even when your pockets aren&amp;#8217;t full! I don&amp;#8217;t need these things!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-seabass2026-sm.jpg" alt="I caught a sea bass! See? Bass! (Why do I keep saying things like that!?)" class="wp-image-6250" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;My fishing haul scored me over 200k yesterday.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I played again today, and Hank was blown away by the fact that I had a salmon. 😆&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-hank-salmon-sm.jpg" alt="Hank: Oh my gosh! You've got a salmon?!" class="wp-image-6251" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;He wanted to trade his pear for it, and I agreed to the exchange. If it makes you &lt;em&gt;that &lt;/em&gt;excited, go enjoy that salmon, Hank. 😆&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I went on my third and final fishing run of September. By the time I was done, I had completely filled up the dump with garbage I&amp;#8217;ve fished from the ocean this week.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-dump2026-sm.jpg" alt="A dump full of garbage fished out of the ocean this September." class="wp-image-6252" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I earned over 300k tonight, which pushed this week&amp;#8217;s total up to one million bells. That was my (unspoken) goal coming in, so I&amp;#8217;m glad I reached that milestone even though the sea bass showed up before I was ready for them. 😆 I should have started earlier in the month, but oh well. &lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;See you all next month!&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/2026/09/11/fishing-for-a-million/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-11T23:48:00-04:00"&gt;September 11, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-09-12T02:01:26-04:00"&gt;September 12, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ac-kiki-out2026-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
